  "notes": [
    "PS1: upstream has one SMT1 dataset (its SmtSnesCompendiumModule). There is no PS1-specific data upstream; these are the SNES-era tables, believed unchanged on PS1 for demons and fusion.",
    "Resistances: upstream's 15-character resist string drops its eighth character (always \"-\"), as upstream's SMT1 module does, leaving 14 elements. Each code decodes to a type and a percent: damage taken for resist/neutral/weak, how much is stopped or returned for null/repel/drain.",
    "Levels keep upstream's decimal tie-breaks (Lakshmi 64.1): fusion level maths uses them; pages print the whole level.",
    "Kinds: Messian and Gaean demons are recruit-only and Machines are enemy-only, as upstream's SMT1 compendium module marks them; upstream sets no other kind.",
    "Special recipes all carry upstream fusion \"normal\", so their results stay in the race chart as well; the app applies the recipe first.",
    "Race alignments come from alignments.json (upstream uses \"D\" for dark races); its \"darks\" map is not read by upstream's SMT1 calculators and is not imported."
  ],
